# Remote Key Provisioning (RKP) — property bridge.
#
# The RedMagic Control toggle writes persist.sys.rm.rkp; init does the actual setprops here.
# It cannot be done from the app: system/sepolicy/private/property.te neverallows every domain
# except init/keystore/shell/system_server/rkpdapp/vendor_init from setting remote_prov_prop, and
# that is a build-time check, not a runtime denial. init is on the permitted list.
#
# These are NOT persist.* properties, so they vanish on reboot. persist.sys.rm.rkp does persist,
# and init re-fires this action when it is loaded at boot, so the setting survives.
#
# Deliberately absent: remote_provisioning.enable_rkpd. It has no exact SELinux context and falls
# back to default_prop. Verified on hardware 2026-09-01 that RKP provisions a full Google-rooted
# chain without it -- the real gate is the device_config flag, which the app sets.
#
# rkpdapp caches the hostname at process start, so the app restarts it after toggling; without
# that it keeps reporting "no default URL" no matter what these properties say.

on property:persist.sys.rm.rkp=1
    setprop remote_provisioning.hostname remoteprovisioning.grapheneos.org
    setprop remote_provisioning.connect_timeout_millis 20000
    setprop remote_provisioning.strongbox.rkp_only true
    setprop remote_provisioning.tee.rkp_only true

on property:persist.sys.rm.rkp=0
    setprop remote_provisioning.hostname ""
    setprop remote_provisioning.strongbox.rkp_only false
    setprop remote_provisioning.tee.rkp_only false
